From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ARM: configs: gts28ltexx: UHID, for Bluetooth keyboards
 and mice

BlueZ creates the input device of a Bluetooth keyboard or mouse through
/dev/uhid: always for LE ones (the HID over GATT profile), and for
classic ones too since UserspaceHID became the default in input.conf
(BlueZ 5.87 on the tablet).  Without UHID no Bluetooth keyboard or
mouse can connect.  Build it in, so /dev/uhid is there when bluetoothd
starts; HIDP stays for UserspaceHID=false.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
index ed177b8bd..4d20651dd 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
@@ -315,6 +315,10 @@ CONFIG_BT_BNEP=m
 CONFIG_BT_BNEP_MC_FILTER=y
 CONFIG_BT_BNEP_PROTO_FILTER=y
 CONFIG_BT_HIDP=m
+# Bluetooth keyboards and mice: BlueZ hands their HID reports to the
+# kernel through /dev/uhid, LE ones always and classic ones by default
+# (input.conf UserspaceHID=true); HIDP above serves UserspaceHID=false.
+CONFIG_UHID=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_DEV_BUS=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_DEV_CTRL_TTYPORT=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_SAMSUNG=m
-- 
2.52.0

